menu "Tab5 Board Support"

choice BSP_TAB5_PANEL
    prompt "Display panel driver"
    default BSP_TAB5_PANEL_AUTO
    help
        The Tab5's MIPI-DSI panel has no I2C presence and no readable ID, so it
        cannot be probed. Auto-detect infers the panel from which touch
        controller answers on I2C, which holds for the board revisions we know
        about but is an inference, not a measurement.

        If your unit boots with working audio and touch but a black screen, the
        inference is wrong for your revision — force the other driver here.

config BSP_TAB5_PANEL_AUTO
    bool "Auto-detect from touch controller"

config BSP_TAB5_PANEL_FORCE_ILI9881C
    bool "Force ILI9881C"

config BSP_TAB5_PANEL_FORCE_ST7123
    bool "Force ST7123"

endchoice

endmenu
